  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`, and it passes `typecheck`. I couldn't run it or `vite build` here, so I haven't seen a rendered frame.\n\n- **Crystals:** There are seven crystals, each built with `geometry.define` and mounted with `geometry.custom`. Each is a 4 to 6 sided prism with a pointed top. Every face has its own vertices, a flat normal and its own colour. Heights, radii and tilts differ.\n- **Cluster and pedestal:** The crystals sit in a `group(\"cluster\")` on a metallic pedestal disc and ground disc. `onFrame` rotates the group slowly about the vertical axis.\n- **Sparks:** One `effects.particles` emitter (additive `spark-streak` sprites) spawns over a disc and drifts upward under weak negative gravity.\n- **Look:** The background is near-black (`#05060c`). Cyan and magenta rim directional lights sit behind the cluster, with a dim blue key light and a violet point light inside it. I added bloom and a vignette.\n- **Setup:** It draws into `#app`. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`.\n\nI didn't add a `looks.preset` or `looks.appOptions`. The scene builds its own dark lighting, as the fire recipe does.\n\nI'm unsure whether `noise: 0.35` on the particle emitter has any visible effect. I passed a plain number because the object form (`strength`, `frequency`) failed `typecheck`.\n\n",
